[{:db/id "q-264754/field-1/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" :answer/id #uuid "bd860533-6dec-57bf-b80a-f38ff42112c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-264754/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "7920a49e-7f15-5858-bd91-d0dee0620c7f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-264754/field-1/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" :answer-field/choices ["q-264754/field-1/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-264754/field-2/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "70648b7f-95e7-53df-ab01-81cd523f0648" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-264754/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "4ef73344-74ee-5489-8f5d-711fb3febee8" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-264754/field-2/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer-field/choices ["q-264754/field-2/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-264754" :question/id #uuid "b7ee32a4-8b6b-5018-a0b9-f3644820a1e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-264754" :question/is-example false :question/problem "In **ascending order,** the solutions of the equation $2{x}^{2}\\cdot {7}^{2x}-50\\cdot {7}^{2x}=0$ are\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}\\cdot {7}^{2x}-50\\cdot {7}^{2x} & =0 \\\\ (2{x}^{2}-50)\\cdot {7}^{2x} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the zero product property, which states that $ab=0$ if and only if $a=0$ or $b=0.$ This gives us two equations,\n\n$$\n2{x}^{2}-50=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{7}^{2x}=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve each of these equations separately.\n\n- The equation $2{x}^{2}-50=0$ can be factored as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2({x}^{2}-25) & =0 \\\\ 2(x-5)(x+5) & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich leads to the solutions $x=-5,5.$\n\n- The equation $2=0$ is not a possible solution because it's a false statement.\n\n- The equation ${7}^{2x}=0$ has no solutions because ${7}^{2x}$ is positive for every real number $x.$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the original equation has the solutions \n\n$$\nx=-5\\,\\text{and}\\,x=5.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-264754/field-1" "q-264754/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3758cf02-ba4b-539a-bc61-8c2030ff6f6f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-264754"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-88459/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "cd36d26a-3ab8-572c-8754-4654c2a157ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88459/selection/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" :answer/id #uuid "594e22ff-8b5e-589a-8daf-251b27267f98" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88459/selection/5d022a88a643e97abec4d01dfce48411101475c0705a98f29f3a8e3560fb0616" :answer/id #uuid "7c26331d-2cee-58be-bca5-0ff24b7d828c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88459/selection/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" :answer/id #uuid "589966ba-6d09-5d2f-8fed-c2579386b944" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88459/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "357ea630-a6e7-550e-add8-97f08f49b8ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88459/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6b2b601a-63c2-5500-84db-f5de16cae5c5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-88459/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer-field/choices ["q-88459/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-88459/selection/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" "q-88459/selection/5d022a88a643e97abec4d01dfce48411101475c0705a98f29f3a8e3560fb0616" "q-88459/selection/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" "q-88459/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-88459" :question/id #uuid "d3d7afbe-c052-55bc-910e-6663c48abfcd" :question/math-academy-id "q-88459" :question/is-example false :question/problem "What is the product of solutions of the equation $2{x}^{2}\\cdot {2}^{x-1}+12x\\cdot {2}^{x-1}+10\\cdot {2}^{x-1}=0?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}\\cdot {2}^{x-1}+12x\\cdot {2}^{x-1}+10\\cdot {2}^{x-1} & =0 \\\\ (2{x}^{2}+12x+10){2}^{x-1} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the zero product property, which states that $ab=0$ if and only if $a=0$ or $b=0.$ This gives us two equations,\n\n$$\n2{x}^{2}+12x+10=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{2}^{x-1}=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve each of these equations separately.\n\n- The equation $2{x}^{2}+12x+10=0$ can be factored as\n\n$$\n2(x+1)(x+5)=0,\n$$\n\nwhich leads to the solutions $x=-5,-1.$\n\n- The equation ${2}^{x-1}=0$ has no solutions because ${2}^{x-1}$ is positive for every real number $x.$\n\nTherefore, the original equation has the solutions $x=-5,-1,$ and their product is $(-5)\\cdot (-1)=5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-88459/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3758cf02-ba4b-539a-bc61-8c2030ff6f6f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-88459"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-100785/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" :answer/id #uuid "a35562a8-74bb-5a5e-85a6-824cea317430" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-100785/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "26dd3863-f500-5882-b2ec-702462991dcc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-100785/selection/5cd5dc93f37c743976373ab57c37b5388ba149bd286c5b2139ed2c89c249424d" :answer/id #uuid "0b37b632-3406-521f-bedf-7e7deb54b0a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-100785/selection/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776" :answer/id #uuid "ee56b96d-cf9c-5ffb-aeec-1a84cbd031a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-100785/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "01b3dbbe-fc62-52ac-a886-a4271bb0f8d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-100785/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ec628ef1-df76-590c-bef8-9536d9150880" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-100785/selection/5cd5dc93f37c743976373ab57c37b5388ba149bd286c5b2139ed2c89c249424d" :answer-field/choices ["q-100785/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" "q-100785/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-100785/selection/5cd5dc93f37c743976373ab57c37b5388ba149bd286c5b2139ed2c89c249424d" "q-100785/selection/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776" "q-100785/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-100785" :question/id #uuid "cc28ec0a-4e61-5f28-bc0a-e54b135917a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-100785" :question/is-example false :question/problem "What is the product of solutions of the equation ${x}^{2}{e}^{9x}-36{e}^{9x}=0?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}{e}^{9x}-36{e}^{9x} & =0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-36){e}^{9x} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the zero product property, which states that $ab=0$ if and only if $a=0$ or $b=0.$ This gives us two equations,\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-36=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{e}^{9x}=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve each of these equations separately.\n\n- The equation ${x}^{2}-36=0$ can be factored as\n\n$$\n(x+6)(x-6)=0,\n$$\n\nwhich leads to the solutions $x=-6,6.$\n\n- The equation ${e}^{9x}=0$ has no solutions because ${e}^{9x}$ is positive for every real number $x.$\n\nTherefore, the original equation has the solutions $x=-6,6,$ and their product is $(-6)\\cdot 6=-36.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-100785/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3758cf02-ba4b-539a-bc61-8c2030ff6f6f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-100785"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-110801/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "7bdd8899-2a26-5acf-a55d-e85d442b403a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110801/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "041305fd-406c-5dea-95be-6318806a78da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110801/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "10bea93c-00d5-5ffa-80aa-93c0e05a8362" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110801/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7bee